# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every
# platform.
#
# Without this a Windows clone checks out CRLF, and since Prettier's endOfLine
# default is "lf", `npm run format:check` then fails on every file in the repo —
# including files nobody has touched. That is the same command CI runs on Linux,
# where the checkout is LF and it passes, so the two disagree for reasons that
# have nothing to do with the code.
#
# `text=auto` still leaves anything Git detects as binary alone; every tracked
# file here is text today.
* text=auto eol=lf
